-- US content 1.4 «domande a scelta» (founder, 28/11/2026): almost every open
-- Gioca prompt becomes multiple choice, with 3 or 4 short options in Italian
-- and English.
--
-- * Converted: the active open prompts of Ridete, Scopritevi, Confrontatevi
--   and Rivivete. Where needed the question is reworded a little so it works
--   as a choice, in its own theme and tone. plus, topic, depth and cooldown
--   stay as they are.
-- * Still open: every longitudinal prompt (re-asked months later with
--   «cosa avevate risposto», through the longitudinal recipe, which only
--   takes open prompts), and the Rivivete prompts that ask for a detail of
--   one precise memory, so Rivivete keeps about 25 open. The question of the
--   day (daily_question_templates) and the couple's own questions
--   (couple_questions) are not in this catalog and do not change. e_se is
--   no longer offered on its own and stays as it is.
-- * Same id, version + 1, as the earlier text fixes (catalog rule: «bump
--   version for a new wording»). Rounds already played keep their own copy
--   (question, answer kind, options) in game_session_items and stay
--   readable; their English, matched on the version they were built from,
--   falls back to the Italian copy, as after every earlier fix. Cooldowns
--   and «già fatte di recente» read the fingerprint 'catalog:<id>' and Play
--   Us reads items by id: neither depends on the version.
-- * The source is supabase/game-v2/content-1-4/games.json; this migration
--   carries the SQL generated from it between the content-1-4 begin/end
--   markers (node scripts/build-content-1-4-sql.mjs), and
--   tests/content-1-4-catalog.test.js fails when the two drift apart.
-- * Every prompt must still be the open wording it replaces (version,
--   Italian, English), or the choice this migration writes: anything else
--   stops the migration before any change. Only updates; nothing is inserted
--   or deleted. Re-applying this migration changes nothing.

-- content-1-4:begin (generated by scripts/build-content-1-4-sql.mjs from supabase/game-v2/content-1-4; do not edit by hand)

-- 141 open prompts become choice: ridete 44, scopritevi 54, confrontatevi 14, rivivete 29.
-- Each line: the wording it replaces (from_version, from, from_en) and the new one.
do $content_1_4$
declare
  changes constant jsonb := $changes$[
{"id":"ridete-001","from_version":3,"from":"Lavoriamo insieme in un ristorante. Chi di noi si farebbe licenziare prima, e perché?","from_en":"We work together in a restaurant. Which of us would get fired first, and why?","question_text":"Lavoriamo insieme in un ristorante. Per cosa ci licenziano dopo una settimana?","options":["Assaggiamo tutto prima di servirlo","Chiacchieriamo coi clienti per ore","Sbagliamo ogni ordine, con stile","Balliamo in cucina in pieno servizio"],"question_text_en":"We work together in a restaurant. What gets us fired within a week?","options_en":["We taste everything before serving it","We chat with customers for hours","We get every order wrong, in style","We dance in the kitchen mid-service"]},
{"id":"ridete-002","from_version":1,"from":"Dobbiamo partecipare a un reality insieme. Quale sarebbe il motivo della nostra prima litigata in diretta?","from_en":"We have to go on a reality show together. What would our first on-camera argument be about?","question_text":"Partecipiamo a un reality insieme. Su cosa battibecchiamo in diretta?","options":["Chi ha finito il caffè","Il lato del letto","Il volume della TV","Chi ha ragione sulla strada"],"question_text_en":"We’re on a reality show together. What do we bicker about on camera?","options_en":["Who finished the coffee","Which side of the bed is whose","The TV volume","Who’s right about the way"]},
